{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-44204","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49688","text":"κ Integration Spec: Product-Level Specification"}]},{"id":"blk-44205","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49689","text":"Version 0.2.0 — Normalized"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44207","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49690","text":"How the cyclicity invariant κ is computed, surfaced, and used across Graphonomous, BendScript, Deliberatic, TickTickClock, and the [&] Protocol.  "},{"id":"spn-49691","marks":["bold"],"text":"v0.2.0 changes (from Codex review):"},{"id":"spn-49692","text":" - Normalized all field names to a single canonical schema (§2.4) - Resolved tool naming: "},{"id":"spn-49693","marks":["code"],"text":"analyze_topology"},{"id":"spn-49694","text":" is the standalone tool; "},{"id":"spn-49695","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-49696","text":" gains a "},{"id":"spn-49697","marks":["code"],"text":"topology"},{"id":"spn-49698","text":" field — no "},{"id":"spn-49699","marks":["code"],"text":"memory_recall_with_topology"},{"id":"spn-49700","text":" tool - Fixed approximation representation: "},{"id":"spn-49701","marks":["code"],"text":"kappa"},{"id":"spn-49702","text":" is always an integer; large SCCs add "},{"id":"spn-49703","marks":["code"],"text":"approximate: true"},{"id":"spn-49704","text":" (no "},{"id":"spn-49705","marks":["code"],"text":"exact"},{"id":"spn-49706","text":" field) - Added instrumentation requirements (§7) - Clarified BendScript directed-edge policy (§4.3)"}]}],"id":"blk-44206","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-44208","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49707","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-44209","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49708","text":"1. Overview"}]},{"id":"blk-44210","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49709","text":"κ (kappa) is a graph-theoretic invariant that measures the minimum irreducible bidirectional information flow in a directed graph. It is the routing primitive that determines whether a query region of a knowledge graph requires single-pass retrieval (κ = 0) or iterative deliberation (κ > 0)."}]},{"id":"blk-44211","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49710","text":"This spec defines:"}]},{"id":"blk-44212","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44214","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49711","text":"How κ is computed"}]}],"id":"blk-44213","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44216","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49712","text":"Where it is computed in the stack"}]}],"id":"blk-44215","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44218","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49713","text":"How it routes inference"}]}],"id":"blk-44217","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44220","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49714","text":"How it is surfaced to users"}]}],"id":"blk-44219","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44222","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49715","text":"How it integrates with each product"}]}],"id":"blk-44221","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-44223","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49716","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-44224","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49717","text":"2. Computation"}]},{"id":"blk-44225","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49718","text":"2.1 Algorithm"}]},{"id":"blk-44226","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"function compute_kappa(graph):\n    # Pre-step: define node universe U from the analyzed subgraph/query result.\n    # Ignore any edge where src ∉ U or dst ∉ U.\n    # Exclude self-loops (u -> u) from adjacency for κ computation.\n    # Step 1: Find all strongly connected components\n    sccs = tarjan_scc(graph)                    # O(V + E)\n\n    # Step 2: For each nontrivial SCC (size > 1)\n    results = []\n    for scc in sccs where |scc| > 1:\n        # Step 3: Enumerate bipartitions, find minimum bidirectional cut\n        k = infinity\n        for (A, B) in nontrivial_bipartitions(scc):\n            edges_a_to_b = count_edges(A, B, graph)\n            edges_b_to_a = count_edges(B, A, graph)\n            bidirectional_cut = min(edges_a_to_b, edges_b_to_a)\n            k = min(k, bidirectional_cut)\n            if k == 0: break  # early exit (can't go lower)\n\n        # Step 4: Record SCC with its κ value and minimum-cut partition\n        results.append({\n            scc: scc,\n            kappa: k,\n            min_cut_partition: (A_min, B_min),\n            min_cut_edges: edges_achieving_minimum\n        })\n\n    return results"},{"id":"blk-44227","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49719","text":"2.2 Complexity"}]},{"id":"blk-44228","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44230","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49720","marks":["bold"],"text":"SCC decomposition:"},{"id":"spn-49721","text":" O(V + E) via Tarjan's algorithm"}]}],"id":"blk-44229","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44232","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49722","marks":["bold"],"text":"κ computation per SCC:"},{"id":"spn-49723","text":" O(2^|SCC| × |SCC|²) in the worst case (enumerating all bipartitions)"}]}],"id":"blk-44231","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44234","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49724","marks":["bold"],"text":"Practical constraint:"},{"id":"spn-49725","text":" For SCCs up to ~20 nodes, bipartition enumeration is feasible in real time. For larger SCCs, use approximation:"}]}],"id":"blk-44233","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44236","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49726","text":"Return SCC size as a proxy for κ, with "},{"id":"spn-49727","marks":["code"],"text":"approximate: true"},{"id":"spn-49728","text":" flag"}]}],"id":"blk-44235","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44238","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49729","text":"κ field remains an integer (the estimate), never a symbol/atom/string"}]}],"id":"blk-44237","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44240","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49730","marks":["bold"],"text":"Node-universe rule (NORMATIVE):"},{"id":"spn-49731","text":" Analyze only the node set supplied by retrieval/query scope (or explicit "},{"id":"spn-49732","marks":["code"],"text":"node_ids"},{"id":"spn-49733","text":" input). Do not pull in external nodes implicitly during κ analysis."}]}],"id":"blk-44239","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44242","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49734","marks":["bold"],"text":"Self-loop rule (NORMATIVE):"},{"id":"spn-49735","text":" Exclude self-loops ("},{"id":"spn-49736","marks":["code"],"text":"source == target"},{"id":"spn-49737","text":") from κ adjacency and cut counts."}]}],"id":"blk-44241","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-44243","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49738","text":"2.3 Incremental Updates"}]},{"id":"blk-44244","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49739","text":"When an edge is added or removed from the knowledge graph:"}]},{"id":"blk-44245","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49740","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-49741","marks":["bold"],"text":"Edge addition:"},{"id":"spn-49742","text":" Can only merge SCCs or enlarge existing ones. Re-run Tarjan on the affected component. If a new nontrivial SCC is formed, compute κ for it. 2. "},{"id":"spn-49743","marks":["bold"],"text":"Edge removal:"},{"id":"spn-49744","text":" Can only split SCCs or shrink them. Re-run Tarjan on the affected component. Recompute κ for any remaining nontrivial SCCs. 3. "},{"id":"spn-49745","marks":["bold"],"text":"Optimization:"},{"id":"spn-49746","text":" Maintain an SCC index alongside the knowledge graph. Incremental SCC algorithms (e.g., Bender, Fineman & Gilbert 2015) can update SCCs in O(V) amortized per edge change."}]},{"id":"blk-44246","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49747","text":"2.4 Canonical Schema (NORMATIVE — all implementations must match)"}]},{"id":"blk-44247","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49748","text":"Every κ topology result — whether from Elixir, JavaScript, or MCP JSON — uses these exact field names:"}]},{"id":"blk-44248","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"sccs\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scc-0\",\n      \"nodes\": [\"node-a\", \"node-b\"],\n      \"kappa\": 2,\n      \"approximate\": false,\n      \"fault_line_edges\": [\n        {\"source\": \"node-a\", \"target\": \"node-b\"}\n      ],\n      \"routing\": \"deliberate\",\n      \"deliberation_budget\": {\n        \"max_iterations\": 3,\n        \"agent_count\": 2,\n        \"timeout_multiplier\": 2.0,\n        \"confidence_threshold\": 0.80\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"dag_nodes\": [\"node-x\", \"node-y\"],\n  \"routing\": \"deliberate\",\n  \"max_kappa\": 2,\n  \"scc_count\": 1\n}"},{"id":"blk-44249","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49749","marks":["bold"],"text":"Field name rules (resolves all drift):"}]},{"id":"blk-44250","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44252","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49750","text":"Top-level routing key: "},{"id":"spn-49751","marks":["code"],"text":"routing"},{"id":"spn-49752","text":" (not "},{"id":"spn-49753","marks":["code"],"text":"overall_routing"},{"id":"spn-49754","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-44251","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44254","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49755","text":"Edge endpoints: "},{"id":"spn-49756","marks":["code"],"text":"source"},{"id":"spn-49757","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-49758","marks":["code"],"text":"target"},{"id":"spn-49759","text":" (not "},{"id":"spn-49760","marks":["code"],"text":"from"},{"id":"spn-49761","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-49762","marks":["code"],"text":"to"},{"id":"spn-49763","text":", not "},{"id":"spn-49764","marks":["code"],"text":"a"},{"id":"spn-49765","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-49766","marks":["code"],"text":"b"},{"id":"spn-49767","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-44253","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44256","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49768","text":"Fault lines: "},{"id":"spn-49769","marks":["code"],"text":"fault_line_edges"},{"id":"spn-49770","text":" (not "},{"id":"spn-49771","marks":["code"],"text":"min_cut_edges"},{"id":"spn-49772","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-44255","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44258","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49773","text":"κ type: always "},{"id":"spn-49774","marks":["code"],"text":"integer"},{"id":"spn-49775","text":" (never string, atom, or symbol)"}]}],"id":"blk-44257","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44260","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49776","text":"Approximation: "},{"id":"spn-49777","marks":["code"],"text":"\"approximate\": true"},{"id":"spn-49778","text":" boolean flag on the SCC object; "},{"id":"spn-49779","marks":["code"],"text":"kappa"},{"id":"spn-49780","text":" still holds the integer estimate"}]}],"id":"blk-44259","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44262","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49781","text":"Routing values: "},{"id":"spn-49782","marks":["code"],"text":"\"fast\""},{"id":"spn-49783","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-49784","marks":["code"],"text":"\"deliberate\""},{"id":"spn-49785","text":" (strings in JSON, atoms "},{"id":"spn-49786","marks":["code"],"text":":fast"},{"id":"spn-49787","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-49788","marks":["code"],"text":":deliberate"},{"id":"spn-49789","text":" in Elixir, strings in JS)"}]}],"id":"blk-44261","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-44263","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49790","marks":["bold"],"text":"Schema boundary rules (NORMATIVE):"}]},{"id":"blk-44264","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44266","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49791","marks":["bold"],"text":"On MCP/JSON boundaries:"},{"id":"spn-49792","text":" use canonical snake_case keys exactly as defined in §2.4 ("},{"id":"spn-49793","marks":["code"],"text":"fault_line_edges"},{"id":"spn-49794","text":", "},{"id":"spn-49795","marks":["code"],"text":"max_kappa"},{"id":"spn-49796","text":", "},{"id":"spn-49797","marks":["code"],"text":"scc_count"},{"id":"spn-49798","text":", etc.)."}]}],"id":"blk-44265","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44268","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49799","marks":["bold"],"text":"Inside Elixir runtime:"},{"id":"spn-49800","text":" atoms are allowed for routing values ("},{"id":"spn-49801","marks":["code"],"text":":fast"},{"id":"spn-49802","text":", "},{"id":"spn-49803","marks":["code"],"text":":deliberate"},{"id":"spn-49804","text":"), but keys remain canonical and are serialized to JSON strings at the boundary."}]}],"id":"blk-44267","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44270","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49805","marks":["bold"],"text":"Inside JavaScript UI code:"},{"id":"spn-49806","text":" camelCase mirrors are allowed for local-only objects ("},{"id":"spn-49807","marks":["code"],"text":"faultLineEdges"},{"id":"spn-49808","text":", "},{"id":"spn-49809","marks":["code"],"text":"maxKappa"},{"id":"spn-49810","text":", "},{"id":"spn-49811","marks":["code"],"text":"sccCount"},{"id":"spn-49812","text":") for ergonomics, but any network payload or persisted topology record must be converted back to canonical snake_case."}]}],"id":"blk-44269","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-44271","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49813","marks":["bold"],"text":"Elixir atom mapping:"}]},{"id":"blk-44272","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"# Elixir uses atoms internally, converts to strings for MCP JSON\n:fast       → \"fast\"\n:deliberate → \"deliberate\""},{"id":"blk-44273","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49814","marks":["bold"],"text":"JavaScript mapping (local only):"}]},{"id":"blk-44274","kind":"code","language":"javascript","text":"// Local object ergonomics\n{ faultLineEdges, maxKappa, sccCount, routing }\n\n// MCP / wire payloads must remain canonical snake_case\n{ fault_line_edges, max_kappa, scc_count, routing }"},{"id":"blk-44275","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49815","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-44276","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49816","text":"3. Routing Logic"}]},{"id":"blk-44277","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49817","text":"3.1 The κ Router"}]},{"id":"blk-44278","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49818","text":"The κ router sits between memory retrieval and reasoning. It inspects the topological structure of the retrieved subgraph and makes a routing decision."}]},{"id":"blk-44279","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"function kappa_route(retrieved_subgraph):\n    scc_analysis = compute_kappa(retrieved_subgraph)\n\n    dag_context = nodes NOT in any nontrivial SCC\n    scc_contexts = scc_analysis  # list of {scc, kappa, fault_line_edges, ...}\n\n    # DAG regions: single-pass retrieval\n    retrieval_context = topological_sort_and_collect(dag_context)\n\n    # SCC regions: flag for deliberation\n    deliberation_tasks = []\n    for scc_info in scc_contexts:\n        deliberation_tasks.append({\n            nodes: scc_info.scc,\n            kappa: scc_info.kappa,\n            fault_lines: scc_info.fault_line_edges,\n            budget: deliberation_budget(scc_info.kappa)\n        })\n\n    return {\n        retrieval_context: retrieval_context,\n        deliberation_tasks: deliberation_tasks,\n        routing: \"fast\" if len(deliberation_tasks) == 0 else \"deliberate\"\n    }"},{"id":"blk-44280","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49819","text":"3.2 Deliberation Budget Function"}]},{"id":"blk-44281","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49820","text":"The deliberation budget maps κ to concrete inference parameters. This is an engineering heuristic (not proved — to be tuned empirically). Caps on "},{"id":"spn-49821","marks":["code"],"text":"max_iterations"},{"id":"spn-49822","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-49823","marks":["code"],"text":"confidence_threshold"},{"id":"spn-49824","text":" are required to prevent runaway values when "},{"id":"spn-49825","marks":["code"],"text":"approximate: true"},{"id":"spn-49826","text":" SCCs use size-based κ estimates:"}]},{"id":"blk-44282","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"function deliberation_budget(kappa):\n    return {\n        max_iterations: min(kappa + 1, 4),\n        agent_count: min(kappa, 3),\n        timeout_multiplier: min(1.0 + 0.5*kappa, 3.5),\n        confidence_threshold: min(0.7 + 0.05*kappa, 0.95)\n    }"},{"id":"blk-44283","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49827","text":"3.3 The Fast Path vs. Deliberation Path"}]},{"id":"blk-44284","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"             ┌─────────────────┐\n             │  Query arrives   │\n             └────────┬────────┘\n                      │\n                      ▼\n             ┌─────────────────┐\n             │  &memory.recall  │   Graphonomous retrieves relevant subgraph\n             └────────┬────────┘\n                      │\n                      ▼\n             ┌─────────────────┐\n             │  κ Router        │   Compute SCCs, κ values\n             └────────┬────────┘\n                      │\n              ┌───────┴────────┐\n              │                │\n         κ = 0 (all DAG)    κ > 0 (has SCCs)\n              │                │\n              ▼                ▼\n       ┌──────────┐    ┌──────────────┐\n       │ Fast Path │    │  Deliberation │\n       │ single    │    │  &reason via  │\n       │ pass      │    │  Deliberatic  │\n       │ retrieval │    │  κ-informed   │\n       └─────┬────┘    │  budget       │\n             │         └──────┬───────┘\n             │                │\n             └───────┬────────┘\n                     │\n                     ▼\n             ┌──────────────┐\n             │  &memory.learn │   Results feed back into graph\n             └──────────────┘"},{"id":"blk-44285","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49828","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-44286","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49829","text":"4. Product Integration"}]},{"id":"blk-44287","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49830","text":"4.1 Graphonomous"}]},{"id":"blk-44288","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49831","marks":["bold"],"text":"Where κ lives:"},{"id":"spn-49832","text":" Computed at query time on the retrieved subgraph. Cached per SCC in the knowledge graph index; invalidated on edge changes."}]},{"id":"blk-44289","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49833","marks":["bold"],"text":"What changes:"}]},{"id":"blk-44290","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44292","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49834","marks":["code"],"text":"Retriever.retrieve/2"},{"id":"spn-49835","text":" now returns a "},{"id":"spn-49836","marks":["code"],"text":"topology"},{"id":"spn-49837","text":" key alongside existing "},{"id":"spn-49838","marks":["code"],"text":"results"},{"id":"spn-49839","text":", "},{"id":"spn-49840","marks":["code"],"text":"causal_context"},{"id":"spn-49841","text":", "},{"id":"spn-49842","marks":["code"],"text":"stats"}]}],"id":"blk-44291","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44294","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49843","text":"New module "},{"id":"spn-49844","marks":["code"],"text":"Graphonomous.Topology"},{"id":"spn-49845","text":" computes and returns the full SCC analysis for a given subgraph"}]}],"id":"blk-44293","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44296","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49846","text":"New function "},{"id":"spn-49847","marks":["code"],"text":"Store.list_edges_between/1"},{"id":"spn-49848","text":" fetches edges within a node set"}]}],"id":"blk-44295","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-44297","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49849","marks":["bold"],"text":"MCP tool: `analyze_topology` (NEW standalone tool):"}]},{"id":"blk-44298","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"name\": \"analyze_topology\",\n  \"description\": \"Compute topological structure (SCCs, κ values, routing decision) for a set of nodes in the knowledge graph.\",\n  \"inputSchema\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"node_ids\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"description\": \"Node IDs to analyze. If omitted, analyzes the full graph.\"\n      },\n      \"query\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"Optional query text. If provided, retrieves relevant nodes first, then analyzes their topology.\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-44299","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49850","marks":["bold"],"text":"MCP tool: `retrieve_context` (EXISTING — augmented with topology):"}]},{"id":"blk-44300","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49851","text":"The existing "},{"id":"spn-49852","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-49853","text":" tool gains a "},{"id":"spn-49854","marks":["code"],"text":"topology"},{"id":"spn-49855","text":" field in its response. No new tool name — same endpoint, richer response:"}]},{"id":"blk-44301","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"query\": \"company strategy\",\n  \"count\": 7,\n  \"results\": [\"...existing results...\"],\n  \"causal_context\": [\"...existing...\"],\n  \"stats\": {\"...existing...\"},\n  \"topology\": {\n    \"sccs\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"scc-0\",\n        \"nodes\": [\"market-share\", \"revenue\", \"r-and-d\", \"product-quality\", \"customer-retention\"],\n        \"kappa\": 1,\n        \"approximate\": false,\n        \"fault_line_edges\": [\n          {\"source\": \"product-quality\", \"target\": \"market-share\"}\n        ],\n        \"routing\": \"deliberate\",\n        \"deliberation_budget\": {\n          \"max_iterations\": 2,\n          \"agent_count\": 1,\n          \"timeout_multiplier\": 1.5,\n          \"confidence_threshold\": 0.75\n        }\n      }\n    ],\n    \"dag_nodes\": [\"founding-date\", \"ceo-name\", \"headquarters\"],\n    \"routing\": \"deliberate\",\n    \"max_kappa\": 1,\n    \"scc_count\": 1\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-44302","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49856","text":"4.2 Deliberatic"}]},{"id":"blk-44303","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49857","marks":["bold"],"text":"What changes:"}]},{"id":"blk-44304","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44306","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49858","text":"Accepts "},{"id":"spn-49859","marks":["code"],"text":"kappa"},{"id":"spn-49860","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-49861","marks":["code"],"text":"fault_line_edges"},{"id":"spn-49862","text":" as input parameters on its deliberation endpoint."}]}],"id":"blk-44305","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44308","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49863","text":"Uses "},{"id":"spn-49864","marks":["code"],"text":"kappa"},{"id":"spn-49865","text":" to set argumentation depth (number of rounds)."}]}],"id":"blk-44307","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44310","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49866","text":"Uses "},{"id":"spn-49867","marks":["code"],"text":"fault_line_edges"},{"id":"spn-49868","text":" (minimum-cut edges) to generate the initial propositions that agents must argue about — these are the critical bidirectional dependencies."}]}],"id":"blk-44309","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-44311","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49869","marks":["bold"],"text":"MCP tool additions:"}]},{"id":"blk-44312","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"name\": \"deliberate_on_scc\",\n  \"description\": \"Run structured argumentation on a strongly connected knowledge cluster. Uses κ to set deliberation budget and fault lines to seed propositions.\",\n  \"inputSchema\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"scc_nodes\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } },\n      \"scc_edges\": { \"type\": \"array\" },\n      \"kappa\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n      \"fault_line_edges\": { \"type\": \"array\" },\n      \"governance\": { \"type\": \"object\" }\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-44313","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49870","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key insight:"},{"id":"spn-49871","text":" Deliberatic doesn't need to know about graph theory. It receives a set of propositions (derived from fault lines), a budget (derived from κ), and it argues. The graph intelligence lives in Graphonomous; the argumentation intelligence lives in Deliberatic. κ is the handshake between them."}]},{"id":"blk-44314","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49872","text":"4.3 BendScript"}]},{"id":"blk-44315","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49873","marks":["bold"],"text":"What changes:"}]},{"id":"blk-44316","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49874","text":"Directed-Edge Policy (NORMATIVE)"}]},{"id":"blk-44317","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49875","text":"BendScript edges have a "},{"id":"spn-49876","marks":["code"],"text":"kind"},{"id":"spn-49877","text":" property. For κ computation, edge directionality is determined by kind:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-44319","spans":[{"id":"spn-49878","text":"Edge kind"}]},{"id":"blk-44320","spans":[{"id":"spn-49879","text":"Directionality for κ"}]},{"id":"blk-44321","spans":[{"id":"spn-49880","text":"Rationale"}]}],"id":"blk-44318","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-44322","spans":[{"id":"spn-49881","marks":["code"],"text":"causal"}]},{"id":"blk-44323","spans":[{"id":"spn-49882","marks":["bold"],"text":"Directed"},{"id":"spn-49883","text":" (a → b)"}]},{"id":"blk-44324","spans":[{"id":"spn-49884","text":"Cause precedes effect"}]}],[{"id":"blk-44325","spans":[{"id":"spn-49885","marks":["code"],"text":"temporal"}]},{"id":"blk-44326","spans":[{"id":"spn-49886","marks":["bold"],"text":"Directed"},{"id":"spn-49887","text":" (a → b)"}]},{"id":"blk-44327","spans":[{"id":"spn-49888","text":"Before precedes after"}]}],[{"id":"blk-44328","spans":[{"id":"spn-49889","marks":["code"],"text":"context"}]},{"id":"blk-44329","spans":[{"id":"spn-49890","marks":["bold"],"text":"Skip"},{"id":"spn-49891","text":" (excluded from κ graph)"}]},{"id":"blk-44330","spans":[{"id":"spn-49892","text":"Symmetric, no feedback"}]}],[{"id":"blk-44331","spans":[{"id":"spn-49893","marks":["code"],"text":"associative"}]},{"id":"blk-44332","spans":[{"id":"spn-49894","marks":["bold"],"text":"Skip"},{"id":"spn-49895","text":" (excluded from κ graph)"}]},{"id":"blk-44333","spans":[{"id":"spn-49896","text":"Symmetric, no feedback"}]}],[{"id":"blk-44334","spans":[{"id":"spn-49897","marks":["code"],"text":"user"}]},{"id":"blk-44335","spans":[{"id":"spn-49898","marks":["bold"],"text":"Skip"},{"id":"spn-49899","text":" (excluded from κ graph)"}]},{"id":"blk-44336","spans":[{"id":"spn-49900","text":"Ambiguous directionality"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-44337","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49901","text":"This is a "},{"id":"spn-49902","marks":["bold"],"text":"hard rule"},{"id":"spn-49903","text":", not a toggle. Only "},{"id":"spn-49904","marks":["code"],"text":"causal"},{"id":"spn-49905","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-49906","marks":["code"],"text":"temporal"},{"id":"spn-49907","text":" edges participate in SCC/κ computation. The filter constant:"}]},{"id":"blk-44338","kind":"code","language":"javascript","text":"const DIRECTED_KINDS = ['causal', 'temporal'];"},{"id":"blk-44339","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49908","text":"Visual Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-44340","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44342","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49909","marks":["bold"],"text":"SCC clusters rendered visually:"},{"id":"spn-49910","text":" Nodes within a nontrivial SCC share a colored halo or background region. Color intensity scales with κ."}]}],"id":"blk-44341","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44344","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49911","marks":["bold"],"text":"Minimum-cut edges highlighted:"},{"id":"spn-49912","text":" Fault-line edges rendered in dashed style ("},{"id":"spn-49913","marks":["code"],"text":"ctx.setLineDash([6, 4])"},{"id":"spn-49914","text":") with brighter color."}]}],"id":"blk-44343","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44346","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49915","marks":["bold"],"text":"κ badge on SCC clusters:"},{"id":"spn-49916","text":" Each SCC cluster shows its κ value as a small badge, e.g., \"κ=2\"."}]}],"id":"blk-44345","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-44347","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49917","text":"Interaction Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-44348","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44350","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49918","marks":["bold"],"text":"Topology preview via context menu:"},{"id":"spn-49919","text":" When the user right-clicks a node and selects \"Connect to…\" (a new context menu item), BendScript shows candidate target nodes with topology impact annotations:"}]}],"id":"blk-44349","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44352","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49920","text":"\"→ NodeX: creates feedback loop (κ: 0→1)\""}]}],"id":"blk-44351","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44354","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49921","text":"\"→ NodeY: strengthens loop (κ: 1→2)\""}]}],"id":"blk-44353","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44356","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49922","text":"\"→ NodeZ: no topological change\""}]}],"id":"blk-44355","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44358","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49923","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"Bend\" action:"},{"id":"spn-49924","text":" Right-click context menu on DAG nodes — automatically suggests the nearest edge that would create a feedback loop."}]}],"id":"blk-44357","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44360","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49925","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"Unbend\" action:"},{"id":"spn-49926","text":" Right-click context menu on SCC nodes — identifies the fault-line edge and offers to remove it."}]}],"id":"blk-44359","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-44361","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49927","marks":["bold"],"text":"Note:"},{"id":"spn-49928","text":" BendScript does NOT currently have drag-to-connect edge creation. The topology preview is accessed via the context menu \"Connect to…\" flow. Do not implement drag-to-connect in this phase."}]},{"id":"blk-44362","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49929","text":"HUD"}]},{"id":"blk-44363","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44365","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49930","marks":["bold"],"text":"Global κ display:"},{"id":"spn-49931","text":" The existing HUD gains a κ readout showing the maximum κ across all SCCs in the graph, and a count of SCCs."}]}],"id":"blk-44364","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44367","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49932","marks":["bold"],"text":"Routing indicator:"},{"id":"spn-49933","text":" \"mode: RETRIEVAL\" (all κ = 0) or \"mode: DELIBERATION\" (any κ > 0)."}]}],"id":"blk-44366","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-44368","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49934","text":"4.4 The [&] Protocol"}]},{"id":"blk-44369","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49935","marks":["bold"],"text":"Grammar extension:"}]},{"id":"blk-44370","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"# Extended [&] capability grammar — topology-aware routing\nTopologyOp      := \"&topology\" \".\" (\"analyze\" | \"route\" | \"kappa\")\n\n# Updated pipeline pattern\nInferencePipeline :=\n    \"&memory.recall\" \"(\" QueryExpr \")\"\n    \"|>\" \"&topology.analyze\" \"()\"\n    \"|>\" \"&topology.route\" \"()\"\n    \"|>\" \"&reason.deliberate\" \"(\" \"budget:\" \":κ\" \")\"\n    \"|>\" \"&memory.learn\" \"()\""},{"id":"blk-44371","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49936","marks":["bold"],"text":"Schema extension (ampersand.schema.json):"}]},{"id":"blk-44372","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"capabilities\": {\n    \"&topology.analyze\": {\n      \"provider\": \"graphonomous\",\n      \"description\": \"Compute SCC decomposition and κ values for a subgraph\",\n      \"config\": {\n        \"max_scc_size_for_exact\": 20,\n        \"approximation_strategy\": \"scc_size_proxy\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"&topology.route\": {\n      \"provider\": \"builtin\",\n      \"description\": \"Route inference based on κ: DAG regions → fast path, SCC regions → deliberation\",\n      \"config\": {\n        \"deliberation_provider\": \"deliberatic\",\n        \"fast_path_provider\": \"graphonomous\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-44373","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49937","text":"4.5 TickTickClock"}]},{"id":"blk-44374","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49938","marks":["bold"],"text":"Connection:"},{"id":"spn-49939","text":" For discrete time-series dynamics, the transition graph of the system has κ > 0 if and only if the system has a periodic orbit. TickTickClock can use this as a formal periodicity detector:"}]},{"id":"blk-44375","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44377","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49940","text":"Discretize time-series data into state transitions"}]}],"id":"blk-44376","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44379","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49941","text":"Build the transition graph"}]}],"id":"blk-44378","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44381","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49942","text":"Compute κ"}]}],"id":"blk-44380","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44383","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49943","text":"κ > 0 → periodic pattern detected, flag for temporal reasoning"}]}],"id":"blk-44382","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44385","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49944","text":"κ = 0 → pure drift, no recurrence"}]}],"id":"blk-44384","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-44386","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49945","text":"This is a secondary integration (TickTickClock already has Mamba SSM for pattern detection), but it provides a complementary structural signal."}]},{"id":"blk-44387","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49946","text":"4.6 OpenSentience"}]},{"id":"blk-44388","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49947","marks":["bold"],"text":"Role:"},{"id":"spn-49948","text":" Research home for the theoretical foundations. Hosts:"}]},{"id":"blk-44389","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44391","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49949","text":"The κ paper (theoretical background, proofs, categorical framework)"}]}],"id":"blk-44390","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44393","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49950","text":"The proof code (runnable verification)"}]}],"id":"blk-44392","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44395","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49951","text":"Interactive demos (live κ computation on user-constructed graphs)"}]}],"id":"blk-44394","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44397","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49952","text":"The original Scale Topology Axis essay (broader theoretical context connecting κ to physics, cosmology, and consciousness science)"}]}],"id":"blk-44396","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-44398","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49953","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-44399","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49954","text":"5. Implementation Priority"}]},{"id":"blk-44400","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49955","text":"Phase 1: Core (ship first)"}]},{"id":"blk-44401","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44403","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49956","text":"[ ] Port κ computation to Elixir (Graphonomous server-side)"}]}],"id":"blk-44402","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44405","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49957","text":"[ ] Port κ computation to JavaScript (BendScript client-side)"}]}],"id":"blk-44404","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44407","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49958","text":"[ ] Integrate Tarjan's SCC into Graphonomous's graph index"}]}],"id":"blk-44406","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44409","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49959","text":"[ ] Return topology annotations from "},{"id":"spn-49960","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"}]}],"id":"blk-44408","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44411","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49961","text":"[ ] Add SCC visualization to BendScript canvas"}]}],"id":"blk-44410","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-44412","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49962","text":"Phase 2: Routing (ship second)"}]},{"id":"blk-44413","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44415","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49963","text":"[ ] Implement κ router in the [&] pipeline"}]}],"id":"blk-44414","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44417","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49964","text":"[ ] Connect κ router to Deliberatic trigger"}]}],"id":"blk-44416","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44419","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49965","text":"[ ] Add deliberation budget function"}]}],"id":"blk-44418","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44421","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49966","text":"[ ] Test on real knowledge graph queries: does κ-aware routing improve answer quality?"}]}],"id":"blk-44420","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-44422","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49967","text":"Phase 3: Polish (ship third)"}]},{"id":"blk-44423","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44425","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49968","text":"[ ] BendScript topology preview via context menu"}]}],"id":"blk-44424","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44427","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49969","text":"[ ] Bend/Unbend context menu actions"}]}],"id":"blk-44426","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44429","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49970","text":"[ ] HUD κ display and routing indicator"}]}],"id":"blk-44428","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44431","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49971","text":"[ ] TickTickClock periodicity detection via κ"}]}],"id":"blk-44430","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44433","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49972","text":"[ ] OpenSentience publication of κ paper and demos"}]}],"id":"blk-44432","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-44434","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49973","text":"Phase 4: Optimization"}]},{"id":"blk-44435","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44437","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49974","text":"[ ] Incremental SCC maintenance (avoid full recomputation on every edge change)"}]}],"id":"blk-44436","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44439","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49975","text":"[ ] Approximate κ for large SCCs (> 20 nodes)"}]}],"id":"blk-44438","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44441","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49976","text":"[ ] Benchmark: latency impact of topology computation on query path"}]}],"id":"blk-44440","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44443","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49977","text":"[ ] A/B test: κ-routed inference vs. uniform retrieval on quality metrics"}]}],"id":"blk-44442","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-44444","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49978","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-44445","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49979","text":"6. Success Metrics"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-44447","spans":[{"id":"spn-49980","text":"Metric"}]},{"id":"blk-44448","spans":[{"id":"spn-49981","text":"Baseline (no κ)"}]},{"id":"blk-44449","spans":[{"id":"spn-49982","text":"Target (with κ)"}]},{"id":"blk-44450","spans":[{"id":"spn-49983","text":"How to Measure"}]}],"id":"blk-44446","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-44451","spans":[{"id":"spn-49984","text":"Answer coherence on circular topics"}]},{"id":"blk-44452","spans":[{"id":"spn-49985","text":"Human eval ~60%"}]},{"id":"blk-44453","spans":[{"id":"spn-49986","text":"Human eval ~80%"}]},{"id":"blk-44454","spans":[{"id":"spn-49987","text":"Blind eval on queries touching SCCs"}]}],[{"id":"blk-44455","spans":[{"id":"spn-49988","text":"Unnecessary deliberation calls"}]},{"id":"blk-44456","spans":[{"id":"spn-49989","text":"N/A (no routing)"}]},{"id":"blk-44457","spans":[{"id":"spn-49990","text":"< 20% of queries"}]},{"id":"blk-44458","spans":[{"id":"spn-49991","text":"Track κ=0 queries that hit deliberation anyway"}]}],[{"id":"blk-44459","spans":[{"id":"spn-49992","text":"Deliberation convergence speed"}]},{"id":"blk-44460","spans":[{"id":"spn-49993","text":"Fixed rounds"}]},{"id":"blk-44461","spans":[{"id":"spn-49994","text":"κ+1 rounds avg"}]},{"id":"blk-44462","spans":[{"id":"spn-49995","text":"Measure rounds to convergence"}]}],[{"id":"blk-44463","spans":[{"id":"spn-49996","text":"User engagement in BendScript"}]},{"id":"blk-44464","spans":[{"id":"spn-49997","text":"Nodes/edges per session"}]},{"id":"blk-44465","spans":[{"id":"spn-49998","text":"+30%"}]},{"id":"blk-44466","spans":[{"id":"spn-49999","text":"Track topology actions (bend/unbend/stargate)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-44467","spans":[{"id":"spn-50000","text":"OpenSentience traffic"}]},{"id":"blk-44468","spans":[{"id":"spn-50001","text":"Baseline"}]},{"id":"blk-44469","spans":[{"id":"spn-50002","text":"Organic from dev community"}]},{"id":"blk-44470","spans":[{"id":"spn-50003","text":"Track referrals from product UIs"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-44471","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50004","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-44472","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-50005","text":"7. Instrumentation Requirements (NEW in v0.2.0)"}]},{"id":"blk-44473","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50006","text":"All κ computation must emit telemetry. This is required for Gate C (performance) and Gate D (product effect) validation."}]},{"id":"blk-44474","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-50007","text":"7.1 Latency Counters (Elixir — "},{"id":"spn-50008","marks":["code"],"text":":telemetry"},{"id":"spn-50009","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-44475","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"# Emit on every topology computation\n# REQUIRED UNIT: duration_ms (float milliseconds)\n# If measured via :timer.tc/1, convert with: duration_ms = duration_us / 1000.0\n:telemetry.execute(\n  [:graphonomous, :topology, :analyze],\n  %{duration_ms: elapsed_ms, node_count: n, edge_count: e},\n  %{scc_count: scc_count, max_kappa: max_kappa, routing: routing}\n)"},{"id":"blk-44476","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50010","text":"Track:"}]},{"id":"blk-44477","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44479","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50011","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.duration_ms"},{"id":"spn-50012","text":" — p50, p95, p99 (canonical latency metric)"}]}],"id":"blk-44478","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44481","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50013","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.node_count"},{"id":"spn-50014","text":" — distribution of subgraph sizes"}]}],"id":"blk-44480","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44483","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50015","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.edge_count"},{"id":"spn-50016","text":" — distribution of subgraph densities"}]}],"id":"blk-44482","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44485","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50017","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.scc_count"},{"id":"spn-50018","text":" — how often SCCs are found"}]}],"id":"blk-44484","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44487","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50019","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.routing.deliberate_ratio"},{"id":"spn-50020","text":" — deliberate / total analyzes"}]}],"id":"blk-44486","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44489","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50021","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.self_loop_filtered_count"},{"id":"spn-50022","text":" — number of self-loops ignored during adjacency construction"}]}],"id":"blk-44488","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-44490","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-50023","text":"7.2 Routing Decision Counters"}]},{"id":"blk-44491","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":":telemetry.execute(\n  [:graphonomous, :topology, :route],\n  %{},\n  %{decision: :fast | :deliberate, max_kappa: max_kappa, trigger: :retrieve_context | :analyze_topology}\n)"},{"id":"blk-44492","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50024","text":"Track:"}]},{"id":"blk-44493","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44495","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50025","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.route.fast_count"},{"id":"spn-50026","text":" — queries routed to fast path"}]}],"id":"blk-44494","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44497","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50027","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.route.deliberate_count"},{"id":"spn-50028","text":" — queries routed to deliberation"}]}],"id":"blk-44496","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-44499","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50029","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.route.deliberate_ratio"},{"id":"spn-50030","text":" — deliberate / total (target: < 30% on typical workloads)"}]}],"id":"blk-44498","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-44500","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-50031","text":"7.3 BendScript Performance (JavaScript — "},{"id":"spn-50032","marks":["code"],"text":"performance.now()"},{"id":"spn-50033","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-44501","kind":"code","language":"javascript","text":"const t0 = performance.now();\nconst topo = analyzeTopology(plane);\nconst elapsed = performance.now() - t0;\nconsole.debug(`[κ] topology: ${elapsed.toFixed(1)}ms, maxκ=${topo.maxKappa}, sccs=${topo.sccCount}`);"},{"id":"blk-44502","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50034","text":"Target: < 50ms at 100 nodes."}]},{"id":"blk-44503","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50035","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-44504","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50036","text":"*Spec version: 0.2.0. Status: Draft (normalized). Depends on: kappa_reference.py (computation), kappa_theory_applied.md (theoretical foundations). Products affected: Graphonomous, Deliberatic, BendScript, [&] Protocol, TickTickClock, OpenSentience.*"}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieravxbzeho6dplqsp67vlojarore5fbo6lj2ileupemymwukfgpljxq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}